ABSTRACT
The Verifiable Agency Theorem assumes a finite state space S and a finite input alphabet Σ.
Neither is specified in A0. This document specifies them.
Without A4, VERIFY has nothing to verify. Preconditions are predicates over state; if state is
undefined, preconditions are undefined. The append-only log has nothing to record. The plan library has no world to plan against. A4 is the premise the entire agentic architecture
rests on.
This document defines:
1. The state schema — what a state is, how it is structured, why it is finite.
2. The world model — how external reality maps into internal state.
3. The sensor interface — how inputs are quantized and delivered.
4. The transition function — how state changes deterministically.
5. The state access protocol — how tiles read and write state.
6. The invariant set — what must always hold.
Every definition is anchored to a requirement of the Verifiable Agency Theorem. Every
constraint is a design decision, not an empirical observation.
Status: This is a specification. No reference implementation exists. No hardware validation
exists.
